From c439f0e58432a24a203986d9d2091bd4e6f23023 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pattex67 <33281022+pattex67@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:08:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Ocarina of Time shader forms; AMD single-return fix for
 discarding programs

Own implementations, after zortos293/Lichii c9ebb5c3af (#87) and Pipe530/Lichii 2c1ad1b12a:
- UISETP and USEL under a UPn guard (guard and old output loaded into the predicate file).
- REDUX signed MIN/MAX; UFLO, UBREV and UPOPC on every uniform register; RED with a uniform
  address of any type (F32 ADD).
- UIMAD with an immediate addend (0x4a4); SEL with a uniform source (0xc07).
- F2I of -Rs; F2IP.U8 of one value (0x243).
- SHF.R.U64 immediate funnel without the U64 bit Maxwell reads as part of the shift.
- ISETP.EX into a free predicate, then PSETP with the accumulated Pc into both destinations.
- In a program with KILL, a Pc-conditional EXIT branches to the closing EXIT (AMD demote
  handling needs one return; the fog pass blacked out the scene).
- SPIR-V FP saturate turns NaN into zero; Maxwell SHR of 32 and more gives 0 (logical) or the
  sign (arithmetic) instead of testing an undefined host result.

Not ported: global UMax32 atomics (need Lichii #47's global atomic helpers), CALL.REL.NOINC
capture change, 64-bit register/uniform right shifts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
